<header><p class="st-kicker">prince bishopric · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Prince-Bishopric of Sion</h1><p class="st-meta">999 CE – 1628 CE · capital Sion</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A prince-bishopric in the Valais, Switzerland, whose bishops held the county granted in 999 until the people of the Upper Valais took power from them.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sion-switzerland">Sion</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> valley, had been a bishopric since the 6th century. In 999 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-iii-of-burgundy">King Rudolf III of Burgundy</a> granted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> the county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valais">Valais</a>, making him a temporal lord. When <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Burgundy</a> passed to the Empire in 1032, the bishops became imperial princes.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> faced the counts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-savoy">Savoy</a>, who held the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valais">Valais</a>, and the growing power of the German-speaking communes (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zenden">Zenden</a>) of the upper valley. Cardinal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthaus-schiner">Matthäus Schiner</a>, bishop from 1499, was a leading diplomat of the Swiss in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a>. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-carolina">Carolina</a> document claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> had granted the county.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The seven <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zenden">Zenden</a> gradually reduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>'s power and in 1613 to 1634 forced bishops to renounce temporal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>, making the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valais">Valais</a> a republic allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/old-swiss-confederacy">Swiss Confederacy</a>. The Valais became a Swiss canton in 1815, and the bishops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sion-switzerland">Sion</a> remain spiritual heads.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="prince bishopric, 999 CE – 1628 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 82 V46 Q50 12 70 46 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 30 V82 M40 58 H60"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">prince bishopric</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:79.58%;width:12.52%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>999 CE – 1628 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>prince bishopric</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sion</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Walter Supersaxo, Matthäus Schiner</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Franco-Provençal, Alemannic German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bishopric of Sion, Sitten</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1314&amp;focus=prince-bishopric-of-sion" aria-label="Prince-Bishopric of Sion on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4854 551 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Prince-Bishopric of Sion lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5174 807L5229 694M5174 807L5174 807"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5174 807h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5174 807h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5174 807h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sion. <a href="/atlas?year=1314&amp;focus=prince-bishopric-of-sion">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
